{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1546566-setting-technology-levels","id":1546566,"title":"Setting Technology Levels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Alchemical Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-03T14:07:36-08:00","id":1546566,"title":"Setting Technology Levels","content":"So, disclaimer, I've read MOST of the manuscript released so far, but haven't fully dissected the Charms and Nations yet, so my question might already be covered. Even still, I am trying to more properly condense and reword it, so that I can grok it more easily.<br /> <br /> So, am I correct in this-- As a whole, Autocthonia is largely a steampunk and dieselpunk setting, tech level wise. Other technology levels exist, but are entirely localized to individual Metropoli based on Municipal Charms. Atom/nukepunk exists, but its a state secret. Cyberpunk is possible, but it would rely on Municipal Charms and thus is limited to Metropoli with them. Cell phones and internet equivalents might exist as part of the design of a single city, or maybe a network of cities. Am I right?<br /> <br /> I do love the setting as it is, and am content with my Steamworld Dig based wild west Nurad location. But I also wanted to contrast it with a sort of pseudo-modern/80s retro neon drenched synth and vaporwave Metropolis, with a &quot;yuppie middle class&quot; and a recently born lawless internet. I think its possible to justify--During the last generation, a Municipal Charm was installed, allowing audiovisual transmission from point to point, birthing radio, television, phones, and a library-database of information. The new generation is learning how to build websites, communicate with other Metropoli with the same Charm, and how to create (and hack) cybersecurity. Nearby cities point at lost Perygra and the Shuttered Lamp war, and worry that the city has gone too far. <br /> <br /> I also worry if I've gone too far, or if the tech level of Autocthonia can be stretched to include those ideas. Is all that possible as RAW?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T13:44:01-08:00","id":1546662,"title":"","content":"I think full on internet might be stretching things a bit.<br /> <br /> Like there's inter-metropolis communication and some degree of broadcasting but nothing on the level of personal access, especially for the populat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T21:08:59-08:00","id":1546828,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I definitely wouldn't go full on modern wikipedia and google levels. I imagine Populat having a sort of myspace page to give them the illusion of property and personalization, with a theme song, likes, small social network.. Maybe rudimentary (tightly regulated) hobby message boards and information centers, some basic educational websites, some rudimentary memes.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I would like some taste of Cyberpunk, but definitely more to an 80s and 90s level as opposed to modern. Enough that a chunk of the Populat works as data analysts, that a yuppie &quot;middle class&quot; exists (which Nurad kinda already has), that cybersecurity and hackers exist, and the like. Populat can call their friends and send emails within the Metropolis and to other Metropoli connected to the Web. Mass media is of course tightly regulated by the Tripartite, but there are three channels with news broadcast and some propaganda rich tv shows with some talk of live news on the horizon. <br /> <br /> Of course, a chunk of the citizenry thinks such things are turning the newest generation's brains into mush and are afraid the whole city is going to be turned to crystal or overrun by Void Hackers. But it also leaves a potential opening for a REALLY unique setting, porting the rules for the Sea of Mind to create a sort of Trinity Anima/Ready Player One/Second Life/Tron city within Autocthon's cybermind. Maybe Perygra isn't gone, it was just uploaded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T06:35:19-08:00","id":1546833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1546566-setting-technology-levels?p=1546828#post1546828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it also leaves a potential opening for a REALLY unique setting, porting the rules for the Sea of Mind to create a sort of Trinity Anima/Ready Player One/Second Life/Tron city within Autocthon's cybermind. Maybe Perygra isn't gone, it was just uploaded.</div> </div> </div> </div>You buried the lede. Idea wasn't really vibing for me, but then I got to this bit, which is super cool.<br /> <br /> Personally I wouldn't want the web to be as ubiquitous as &quot;everyone has an email address&quot;. I would lean into earlier cyberpunk when computers were still &quot;terminals&quot; and &quot;mainframes&quot;, and getting access to the web was something you'd have to do at work or, perhaps, in a public library.<br /> <br /> Then, some metaphysical catastrophe happens and a bunch of minor information-spirits end up in tight quarters with the human population and start forming symbiotic relationships with individual humans (acting a little like Shadowrun PANs)<br /> <br /> Then in the second-act twist, it turns out that the PANs, the municipal web, or both are Void spirits and Oasis is either secretly a front for the nightmare hellscape they're trying to trap everyone in, OR the place the players have to team up to defend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T10:48:02-08:00","id":1546846,"title":"","content":"Autochthonia at its best is very analogue in form and function, and whatever kind of approximation of modern information technology one comes up with isn't going to be available to most of the Populat as a matter of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T17:59:19-08:00","id":1546852,"title":"","content":"I could probably work with that. My setting plan is a stand in for &quot;modern&quot; Exalted, with a neon drenched 80s vibe. The idea does sort of rely on the &quot;middle class&quot; that is unique to the Metropolis that I've been brainstorming. Essentially, it expands a bit on Nurad's more fluid social castes. Shift Chiefs, Supervisors, and Vocants of the Populat and newly graduated Tripartites have roughly the same privelage, with small apartments in trendy neighborhoods and some spending credit to throw around. Some pool their credit with friends or a partner to get a private home in the suburbs, especially if they have a remote job in data analysis or the like. These are the folks who would have their own private email addresses and home terminals, as &quot;snail mail&quot; can't be efficiently scanned for sedition or heresy as easily and wastes physical resources. The rest of the populat is informed by their Foremen and access VERY limited internet at the Library, for sure, though having private chiptune players for leisure time is allowed.<br /> <br /> And of course, all of this is borderline heresy, if not actually heresy. While the Nuradi central Tripartite hasn't banned anything they're up to, they most certainly have spies installed to make sure the line isn't crossed. Older folks in the Metropolis wrinkle their noses as all of this, calling the youth brain rotted and weak. And a chunk of the people fear what happens when the economic boom slows down, or data-conduits run dry, are hacked by Voidbringers, imbalanced resource management results in true capitalism, or Autocthon makes the city the next Perygra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-13T12:16:29-08:00","id":1547717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1546566-setting-technology-levels#post1546566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, am I correct in this-- As a whole, Autocthonia is largely a steampunk and dieselpunk setting, tech level wise. Other technology levels exist, but are entirely localized to individual Metropoli based on Municipal Charms. Atom/nukepunk exists, but its a state secret. Cyberpunk is possible, but it would rely on Municipal Charms and thus is limited to Metropoli with them. Cell phones and internet equivalents might exist as part of the design of a single city, or maybe a network of cities. Am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, having finally gotten to the Technology and Artifacts chapter, I want to address this question in a bit more depth than focusing on the whole internet thing.<br /> <br /> So the presentation of the Octet seems to be that, as far as technology that penetrates into most people's lives, the Octet is not actually that far removed from Creation; keeping in mind that Creation can have fairly sophisticated manufactured items (things like a large scale of plumbing are a possibility), most people in the Eight Nations are going to engage with these things on the level of the tools that they use and buildings they're exposed to. Most of that isn't even going to be fantastical, just manufactured at large scale and intensity because the necessities of life in the Realm of Brass and Shadows requires it constantly, and between the Alchemical Exalted and any systems of the Maker they can jury rig, they can provide a lot of motive force that things like wind and water power would not do as well. Likewise, most of what people do on their off-hours are not very high-tech, as it's mostly services provided by people.<br /> <br /> But it also has areas where it spikes up. Municipal Charms are one thing, pervasive wonders of inhabiting an elder Champion. Many of these upscale the manufacturing capacity of the polis, or provide protection against some environmental hazard, but there are also many where their form and function is a lot less prosaic. There's a technological edge to them, but I think they also often need to be seen through the lens of the personality of the actual Exalt behind them. A Charm-based citywide network for communication isn't quite going to resemble conventional telecommunications, because it's an expression of the Exalt's acts of communication.<br /> <br /> It's also apparent from the aforementioned chapter that, between the resources of their world and expertise of people within it, they have a capacity to make items that have a fantastical quality to them, but are not outright magical in nature as an Artifact is. Some steampunk aesthetic is in there, but the game is not limiting itself to that, so you can get things like luminscent gels or eye glasses whose lenses are made from special crystal to make them quite good at protection from intense light sources or visibility in darkness. There's an emphasis there on &quot;ingenuity plus good manufacturing tools plus a lot of resources harvested from the body of God can let you make some pretty neat objects with sophisticated functions&quot;. The presence of these in the lives of most Autochthonians is probably mostly going to be ad hoc as their work requires, but sometimes (particularly in the more prosperous nations) provided to broaden the range of quality of life (so long as it does not subvert the rigidity of the state).<br /> <br /> Still, sometimes the confluence of these things mean you can get a city where criminals are zooming around on motorised bicycles or self-driving palanquins having running crossbow fights.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-19T10:11:10-08:00","id":1547832,"title":"","content":"I've found something that's useful to keep in mind with Autochthonia: some instances of technology might be machine spirits and similar entities that can be persuaded to fulfil specialist jobs.<br /> <br /> For example, instead of a cell phone as a commercial product people own, something that's more like a Mother Box\u2014not in terms of power but in it being a sentient being that's partnered with a human handler and helps with a variety of tasks in exchange for basic mobility and interpersonal engagement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T09:48:17-08:00","id":1547910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1546566-setting-technology-levels?p=1547832#post1547832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, instead of a cell phone as a commercial product people own, something that's more like a Mother Box\u2014not in terms of power but in it being a sentient being that's partnered with a human handler and helps with a variety of tasks in exchange for basic mobility and interpersonal engagement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that makes sense as something that a sorcerer might do, or an ad hoc relationship that an Exalted or other adventurer might develop (the former particularly if it should be their actual familiar), but not something conventional in the setting by way of being discouraged by the Theomachracy (and perhaps the actual divine hierarchy) and kind of risky in any event.<br /> <br /> Particularly in this Edition that seems to be leaning more heavily into the idea that the spirits of Autochthonia are hardly distinguishable from demons. That Mother Box had an original function in the anatomy of the Maker or the service of Second and Third Circle Souls, and while they still have a form of personal will it might still affect priorities in a way that does not always rest comfortably alongside human habitation.<br /> <br /> In any case, I think making something work by sticking a spirit in it is a can that should be handled cautiously, because otherwise it feels like it would be the most basic go to option for functional results.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T12:33:07-08:00","id":1547917,"title":"","content":"It's pretty extreme, but perhaps less so than a personal mobile phone with all the associated infrastructure required and some significant cultural implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-25T12:45:01-08:00","id":1547949,"title":"","content":"Suddenly I'm picturing people being able to requisition these little speaking tube horns that come with little cables that can be hooked up to points made fairly ubiquitous throughout a city by a Municipal Charm that facilitates locating a specific intended other person who'll hear the chiming of the nearest point they can connect their own tube to speak through.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't even discount it having some element of translating sound into electrical signals, but where the core infrastructure still resembles a big tangled mass of pipes (somewhat evocative of an organ) as well as wires, and there's an understanding that at least part of the transition is being facilitated by Essence. But still.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't exactly translate to the social context of actual phones from the fact that you can't typically own such things personally, but at the same time the whimsy of the Alchemical puts a lot of influence on local authorities to release the horns for reasons more than the solely pragmatic, and there's a degree to which the Exalt actually is trying to encourage a distinct cultural emergence from having such means to talk to people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}